          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"salt-and-pepper-noise-min-max-and-median-filters\">Salt-and-pepper noise: min, max, and median filters</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This animation shows how local neighborhood filters operate on an\n8-bit grayscale image containing salt-and-pepper noise.</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Min filter:</strong> suppresses bright salt pixels.</li>\n<li><strong>Max filter:</strong> suppresses dark pepper pixels.</li>\n<li><strong>Median filter:</strong> suppresses both while usually preserving edges\n  better than min/max filtering.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The red square marks the current filter position. The middle panel\nshows the neighborhood values, and the right panel shows the result\nbeing built progressively.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
